From 5c2955e4b70691aa4af63b322775939244937d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:53:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] A17 LineageParts: build against a base without the LineageOS
 framework

LineageParts comes from lineage-23.2 and calls five things the
LineageOS framework adds to frameworks/base, none of which the Android 17
base this image pins has:

  Settings.System.ACCELEROMETER_ROTATION_ANGLES  (DisplayRotation)
  Settings.System.VOLUME_KEY_CURSOR_CONTROL      (ButtonSettings)
  AbsSeekBar.updateTouchProgress, overridden     (BacklightTimeoutSeekBar)
  DevicePolicyManager.requireSecureKeyguard()    (SetupActionsFragment)
  com.android.internal.os.DeviceKeyHandler       (atv/ and gestures/)

The image shipped LineageParts anyway, because its compiled classes
dated from July and every incremental build since reused them. The
DeviceKeyHandler interface was a file copied into the checkout by hand,
which no manifest or patch recreated. The first build that recompiled
LineageParts failed with six "cannot find symbol" errors.

The two settings keys are spelled out, as the compiled app already had
them inlined. The seek bar method stays, with no @Override, since nothing
calls it on this base. requireSecureKeyguard makes the LineageOS
framework's three tests from public DevicePolicyManager calls. The
interface is declared in the app, where the hand-copied file had it.
Behaviour matches the image that shipped, except that opening a
profile's actions no longer throws NoSuchMethodError.
---
 .../android/internal/os/DeviceKeyHandler.java | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../hardware/DisplayRotation.java             |  8 +++++--
 .../input/BacklightTimeoutSeekBar.java        |  3 ++-
 .../lineageparts/input/ButtonSettings.java    |  8 +++++--
 .../profiles/SetupActionsFragment.java        | 17 +++++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/internal/os/DeviceKeyHandler.java

diff --git a/src/com/android/internal/os/DeviceKeyHandler.java b/src/com/android/internal/os/DeviceKeyHandler.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..992f70a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/com/android/internal/os/DeviceKeyHandler.java
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+/*
+ * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: The LineageOS Project
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+ */
+
+package com.android.internal.os;
+
+import android.view.KeyEvent;
+
+/**
+ * Device-specific key handler interface.
+ *
+ * The LineageOS framework declares this interface, and PhoneWindowManager hands key events to a
+ * device's implementation of it. The Android 17 base this image builds on does not declare it,
+ * and the image configures no device key handler (config_deviceKeyHandlerLib/Class are empty), so
+ * LineageParts' atv/ and gestures/ KeyHandler classes are never loaded. They still name the type,
+ * so it is declared here and compiled into LineageParts.apk. No framework copy exists to clash
+ * with it.
+ */
+public interface DeviceKeyHandler {
+    KeyEvent handleKeyEvent(KeyEvent event);
+}
